## Change review - 2026-10-28

**OAuth administration separates spend identity but needs semantic filter validation.** Reviewed commit `50e64f3be7cc7adb2dc4966b4381296cf4739faa` (commit date `2026-10-22T11:03:55-07:00`). Compared with `922fd9ba79a64a957f8e99cc3e9efaecf8f209c7`; the complete Git comparison contains 269 changed paths.

The inspected generated OAuth-client models distinguish authentication client_id from ai_gateway.usage_client_id, an opaque case-sensitive billing/limit identity that must not be derived from client_id. They expose public/confidential client type, grant types, redirect URIs and active state. The filter contract has an actionable inconsistency: its comments restrict supported field/operator to is_active/EQUALS, while the generated operator enum accepts NOT_EQUALS and ordered comparisons and the field remains an unrestricted string. Therefore schema acceptance alone cannot establish server-supported query semantics. The generated GET mock checks bearer/accept/user-agent headers and returns an inactive static client; that fixture does not exercise revocation enforcement, tenant authorization or billing-ID mapping. Python uses Pydantic models, optional metadata and an open client-type enum, with serializers omitting absent optional fields.

Evidence: [src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclient.py:1-120](https://github.com/gleanwork/api-client-python/blob/50e64f3be7cc7adb2dc4966b4381296cf4739faa/src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclient.py#L1-L120) · [src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclienttype.py:1-14](https://github.com/gleanwork/api-client-python/blob/50e64f3be7cc7adb2dc4966b4381296cf4739faa/src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclienttype.py#L1-L14) · [src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclientfilter.py:1-61](https://github.com/gleanwork/api-client-python/blob/50e64f3be7cc7adb2dc4966b4381296cf4739faa/src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclientfilter.py#L1-L61) · [src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclientaigateway.py:1-23](https://github.com/gleanwork/api-client-python/blob/50e64f3be7cc7adb2dc4966b4381296cf4739faa/src/glean/api_client/models/platformoauthclientaigateway.py#L1-L23) · [tests/mockserver/internal/handler/pathgetapiadminoauthclientsclientid.go:1-74](https://github.com/gleanwork/api-client-python/blob/50e64f3be7cc7adb2dc4966b4381296cf4739faa/tests/mockserver/internal/handler/pathgetapiadminoauthclientsclientid.go#L1-L74).

**Harness consequence:** At the Glean adapter boundary preserve authentication and spending identities separately, validate the documented semantic subset and expose unknown client variants without inferring permissions. Add boundary fixtures for unsupported operators, missing billing identity and inactive clients before enabling administrative operations. These SDKs remain transport references, not a replacement for versioned evidence storage or proof of service-side authorization.

**Scope and limits:** Scoped static inspection of generated OAuth-client contracts and one generated HTTP fixture within the enumerated change inventory. Other changed APIs, retries, streaming helpers and dependency generation were not audited. No SDK tests, Glean account, live authorization, search quality or subscription eligibility was exercised. Historical inventory-screening limitations remain outside this slice.

